@startuml
title TMFC036 : Lead and Opportunity Management -- eTOM/SID ABE Links

class "L2 - Contact/Lead/Prospect Management" as ContactLeadProspectManagement <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "L2 - Selling" as Selling <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "L2 - Market Sales Support & Readiness" as MarketSalesSupportReadiness <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "Sales Lead" as SalesLead <<SID Data Entity>>
class "Sales Opportunity" as SalesOpportunity <<SID Data Entity>>

' eTOM activity <-> SID ABE links. Per the image's own legend, an arrow from the
' eTOM activity towards the SID ABE means information produced by the activity;
' the reverse arrow means information consumed by the activity. The image draws
' each of these four pairs as a single double-headed arrow, i.e. both hold
' simultaneously.
ContactLeadProspectManagement --> SalesLead : produces
SalesLead --> ContactLeadProspectManagement : is consumed by

MarketSalesSupportReadiness --> SalesOpportunity : produces
SalesOpportunity --> MarketSalesSupportReadiness : is consumed by

Selling --> SalesLead : produces
SalesLead --> Selling : is consumed by

Selling --> SalesOpportunity : produces
SalesOpportunity --> Selling : is consumed by

@enduml
